failure_modes.text:
## 32. Product / utility failure potential
Failure risk is low because these are local snippets, but some utilities could produce wrong results or fail on edge cases:
- empty-string indexing;
- duplicated unmatched tokens;
- substring-based stop detection;
- missing `BigInt` dependency;
- integer overflow/negative handling gaps.

If reused blindly in production code, snippet provenance and contract ambiguity would become a significant reliability risk.

